from pathlib import Path
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent/'stage/d851d9ba11a1/astraupskill'
additions={
'README.md': '''Use this as a small service-review workshop. First predict the output of a SUBMITTED deal changing to SALES_APPROVED. Then run the lab and compare its history payload to your prediction. Next change the actor from SALES_REP to PARTNER_SELLER and explain the refusal using the actual permission helper. Finally examine an audit failure and distinguish attempted calls from committed records. These are separate learning methods: prediction, executable feedback, code tracing and failure analysis. No production behavior was changed. The database and repositories are adapters; actual policy, errors and quarter formatting execute from source. Read [the test](../tests/deal-transition-lab.test.mjs) with [the service](../src/services/dealRegistrationService.ts), then attempt the exercises before the answers.''',
'01-CODEBASE-MAP.md': '''The repository is `src/repositories/dealRepository.ts`, not a second transition service. Its visibility query combines the deal id with `buildOwnedRecordVisibilityFilter`. Its update query, however, selects only by id; it does not include the previously observed status. This distinction matters when two callers read the same status before either writes. The harness replaces repository operations, so visibility SQL and update predicates are inspected source facts, not executed database evidence. `src/lib/time.ts` formats the quarter for the queued job; that real helper is loaded. `src/lib/errors.ts` supplies statusCode-bearing errors. Follow an id across the service, approval history and job payload to understand how these records relate without confusing their different purposes.''',
'02-CONCEPTS.md': '''Consider two sales representatives reading SUBMITTED concurrently. Each policy check can pass before either transaction starts. Grouping writes into transactions does not by itself compare the old status at write time. A conditional update containing expected status, a version column, or an appropriate locking design could address this; each requires provider-backed tests. The current lab deliberately does not implement that redesign. Approval history records who attempted which transition with a note, while an audit event supports operational investigation. Neither record should be described as a lock. The queued leaderboard job is another persisted request; inserting it does not prove a worker ran or a leaderboard changed. Separating these concepts prevents a junior developer from mistaking a successful service return for completion of every downstream effect.''',
'03-WORKED-CHANGE.md': '''For a concrete trace, use deal d1, actor u1, note reviewed, and next status SALES_APPROVED. The update payload identifies d1 and the new status. History includes fromStatus SUBMITTED, toStatus SALES_APPROVED, actorUserId u1 and the note. The audit action is deal.transitioned. The returned value is the updated repository record. For SALES_APPROVED to APPROVED under CHANNEL_MANAGER, the job adds type LEADERBOARD_REFRESH, status QUEUED, sourceEntity DealRegistration and sourceEntityId d1. Its quarter follows the real year-Q-number formatter. These assertions check meaningful data, rather than merely counting calls. Compare them with [the executable fixture](../tests/deal-transition-lab.test.mjs). The unchanged production source is retained as a reference snapshot for later experiments.''',
'04-TESTING-AND-DEBUGGING.md': '''Run `node --experimental-vm-modules --test tests/deal-transition-lab.test.mjs` from the project directory. If a permission case unexpectedly enters the transaction, inspect the real domain edge and role map rather than adding a fake permissions array to the session. If history lacks the note, inspect the service fallback from note to rejectionReason. If a job is unexpectedly scheduled after an audit error, compare the awaited sequence. The injected error object must propagate unchanged, so an identity assertion catches accidental wrapping or swallowing. A separate database test would force audit insertion to fail and then query persisted status and history using another connection. Only that provider test can substantiate rollback. Do not alter the adapter to simulate rollback and present the result as database proof.''',
'05-PRACTICE.md': '''Exercise A: draw a sequence diagram for d1 moving from SUBMITTED to SALES_APPROVED by u1. Label the pre-read and transaction boundary, then write the expected approval payload. Exercise B: switch the actor to PARTNER_SELLER without changing state; predict the HTTP-intent code and first forbidden call. Exercise C: have CHANNEL_MANAGER request APPROVED directly from SUBMITTED; distinguish the state error from the role error. Exercise D: inject failure at update, then at audit, and compare the final attempted operation. Exercise E: design a race test for two approvals using independent database connections. State whether your proposed version check belongs in the repository predicate or in a prior service read. Grade each answer on exact source names, trace order, payload fields and honest evidence limits.''',
'06-SOLUTIONS-AND-REVIEW.md': '''For Exercise A, history contains d1, u1, SUBMITTED, SALES_APPROVED and reviewed; no leaderboard job is created. Exercise B returns statusCode 403 before tx. Exercise C returns 409 for the invalid edge, also before tx. A missing visible deal returns 404. Exercise D stops at update for the first injected failure, and reaches update plus approval before failing at audit in the second; the APPROVED job is not reached. Exercise E must coordinate reads and writes with barriers, not sleeps, and verify persisted records from another connection. A version or expected-status predicate must be checked at mutation time to detect a stale observation. These are design exercises, not changes delivered by this course. Reviewers should distinguish an awaited transaction callback from an observed successful commit.''',
'07-TRACE-LAB.md': '''Build a worksheet with columns for operation, input, client identity, returned value and failure outcome. For sales approval, fill find, tx, update, approval and audit. For channel approval, append job and record its source id and quarter. The refusal matrix contains PARTNER_SELLER requesting sales approval (403), a direct SUBMITTED to APPROVED jump (409), and an absent visible deal (404). All three show find as the only recorded operation. In the update failure row, approval must be absent. In the audit failure row, job must be absent. Compare your worksheet to call arrays in the runtime lab, then mark each row as observed through an adapter or executed pure policy. This final annotation prevents a sequence diagram from becoming an unsupported claim about database durability.''',
'VERIFICATION.md': '''Run `node --experimental-vm-modules --test tests/deal-transition-lab.test.mjs` from this project. Five test cases contain multiple scenarios: sales success, channel success with job, a combined refusal matrix, update failure and audit failure. The refusal matrix itself checks role denial, illegal adjacency and missing deal. Real authorization, workflow rules, error classes and quarter formatting are loaded, with an unused ZodError export adapted at the external package boundary. Repository, transaction, audit and job persistence are explicit adapters. The assertions verify payload fields, ordering, error identity and reuse of the supplied client. They do not execute visibility queries or status-update SQL. Source inspection found the update selects only by id, while visibility and state are read earlier. Full typechecking, provider isolation, rollback, concurrent approval and worker execution remain outside the captured check.''',
}
for name,extra in additions.items():
 p=P/name;t=p.read_text();t=t.split('\n\nReview the named source call')[0]
 t=t.replace('Root?s captured','The captured').replace('test?s',"test's").replace('?admin?', 'admin').replace('?fix?','fix')
 t=t.replace('The pre-read being outside the transaction is a deliberate architecture fact, not an omission to fix in this lab.','The pre-read is outside the transaction; inspect the resulting stale-read risk before proposing a change.')
 if name=='VERIFICATION.md':t=t.replace('sales approval, channel approval job, role or invalid-edge refusal, missing deal, and update/audit failures','sales approval, channel approval job, combined refusals, update failure and audit failure')
 p.write_text(t+'\n\n'+extra+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
